WEBVTT

00:00:18.114 --> 00:00:26.644
Kanashimi ikuta noseshi fune

00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:38.834
Horobi no uta no koe takaku

00:00:43.644 --> 00:00:48.164
Kuraki soko yori

00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:54.704
Ukabi koshi

00:00:58.684 --> 00:01:09.824
Aa kimi to ima shirogane o nuke

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:21.574
Ozora e futari tobu hi no

00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:35.754
Kuru o yume min, kuru o yume min

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.544
Miss Wakatake? Miss Wakatake?

00:02:38.884 --> 00:02:41.724
Miss Wakatake! Wake up!

00:02:49.734 --> 00:02:53.664
Um... it's time for school!

00:02:55.004 --> 00:02:56.694
What?!

00:02:58.574 --> 00:03:00.004
Doubt.

00:03:05.914 --> 00:03:08.784
One breakfast, please!

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:10.354
Yes, dear!

00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:12.374
You certainly took your time, hon!

00:03:12.624 --> 00:03:13.954
Thank you!

00:03:16.054 --> 00:03:17.994
Time to eat!

00:03:21.164 --> 00:03:24.194
Are you the new student who came yesterday?

00:03:24.734 --> 00:03:27.864
Now, no need to rush. Eat up!

00:03:28.134 --> 00:03:29.574
Okay!

00:03:29.574 --> 00:03:30.834
Thank you!

00:03:31.704 --> 00:03:33.174
Bye, now!

00:03:33.974 --> 00:03:35.344
See you!

00:03:35.344 --> 00:03:37.004
Have a good day!

00:03:50.924 --> 00:03:54.154
Looks like you got a good night's sleep!

00:03:54.694 --> 00:03:55.934
Yes!

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:58.024
Well, that's good!

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.764
Time to eat!

00:04:06.444 --> 00:04:08.274
Is something wrong?

00:04:09.274 --> 00:04:11.334
No, nothing!

00:04:12.584 --> 00:04:13.984
Looking for Hagino?

00:04:16.014 --> 00:04:22.484
She's long gone. She's not the type to ever
oversleep... unlike some people!

00:04:24.024 --> 00:04:25.824
I wasn't looking for her!

00:04:42.974 --> 00:04:44.574
You've gotta be kidding!

00:04:48.714 --> 00:04:50.814
Oh no! We've got to go!

00:04:51.184 --> 00:04:52.654
But how come?

00:04:59.524 --> 00:05:02.364
Seniors have flexible schedules.

00:05:02.994 --> 00:05:05.554
And I'm repeating my junior year.

00:05:06.164 --> 00:05:09.334
I don't have to take the classes
I've already passed.

00:05:10.474 --> 00:05:11.974
Let's go!

00:05:11.974 --> 00:05:13.044
Okay!

00:05:13.044 --> 00:05:14.304
Thank you!

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:16.544
Here's your lunch!

00:05:17.844 --> 00:05:19.644
Thank you, Ma'am!

00:05:19.914 --> 00:05:21.404
See you!

00:05:22.054 --> 00:05:24.414
Take care, now!

00:05:24.484 --> 00:05:26.854
She sure starts the day at top volume.

00:05:41.304 --> 00:05:43.064
Blue to Commander.

00:05:43.904 --> 00:05:51.904
Current performance recovery rate is 74%. Last
night's Leminof Shift hasn't affected the ship.

00:05:53.914 --> 00:05:57.884
The summons was sudden, so it took some
work to get everything ready,

00:05:57.884 --> 00:06:01.114
but my own shift should be possible soon, too.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.114
Good work.

00:06:03.324 --> 00:06:08.554
It's been a long wait, but we'll be able
to resume operations soon.

00:06:11.604 --> 00:06:15.234
No. I'd like to hold off a little bit.

00:06:16.204 --> 00:06:21.374
But with the ship almost repaired, if we don't
resume our investigation immediately,

00:06:21.374 --> 00:06:23.974
Arume's bound to...

00:06:24.084 --> 00:06:28.744
I know. Wait for my orders to move.

00:06:29.714 --> 00:06:30.924
Commander...

00:06:30.924 --> 00:06:33.284
If this is about the accident...

00:06:35.124 --> 00:06:36.484
Tsubael.

00:06:37.394 --> 00:06:41.484
I'm sorry. Please give me more time to think.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:45.394
Forgive me. Signing off.

00:06:53.444 --> 00:06:56.904
What's wrong with me?

00:07:15.464 --> 00:07:16.564
11th Grade Cherry Blossoms

00:07:16.564 --> 00:07:20.804
11th Grade Cherry Blossoms
And so, Mari Wakatake will
be joining our class today.

00:07:21.534 --> 00:07:24.904
Miss Wakatake, please introduce
yourself to the class.

00:07:26.174 --> 00:07:28.874
I'm Mari Wakatake.

00:07:35.684 --> 00:07:39.554
Pleased to meet you.

00:07:42.894 --> 00:07:45.194
Er... is that all?

00:07:45.464 --> 00:07:46.924
Yes.

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:53.604
Miss Wakatake has lived with her
grandmother for a long time.

00:07:53.604 --> 00:07:59.504
She's never attended school before, so I'd like
all of you to help answer her questions.

00:08:01.544 --> 00:08:04.244
Now, where should you sit?

00:08:05.114 --> 00:08:07.944
I know... over by Miss Senkoji,
our class chairperson.

00:08:09.284 --> 00:08:13.054
You'll look after her, won't you, Miss Senkoji?

00:08:13.184 --> 00:08:14.454
Yes, Ma'am.

00:08:14.454 --> 00:08:16.154
Oh, great.

00:08:23.164 --> 00:08:25.794
Good morning, Miss Wakatake.

00:08:27.474 --> 00:08:31.404
All right, everyone! Let's all work hard today!

00:08:33.244 --> 00:08:37.974
Green, green grows the spring willow.
But never plant it in your garden.

00:08:38.844 --> 00:08:42.514
Never pick a falsehearted man for a friend.

00:08:43.114 --> 00:08:47.954
Although the willow may bud early, does it
hold up when autumn's first wind blows?

00:08:48.754 --> 00:08:53.524
A falsehearted man makes friends easily,
but he is fickle.

00:08:54.994 --> 00:08:58.834
Whereas the willow for many springs
takes on new color,

00:08:58.834 --> 00:09:02.864
a falsehearted man will break off
with you and never call again.

00:09:03.134 --> 00:09:06.104
In the province of Harima in the town of Kako

00:09:06.104 --> 00:09:08.474
there dwelt a scholar whose name
was Hasebe Samon.

00:09:08.474 --> 00:09:13.644
All right, that's good.
Please continue... Wakatake.

00:09:13.984 --> 00:09:16.114
Wakatake? Are you there?

00:09:16.454 --> 00:09:18.084
Hey, Wakatake!

00:09:18.084 --> 00:09:19.584
Miss Wakatake!

00:09:19.584 --> 00:09:20.884
Wakatake!

00:09:23.454 --> 00:09:24.854
Start here.

00:09:29.634 --> 00:09:33.764
He lived a poor but honest life, and except for
the books that kept him company

00:09:33.764 --> 00:09:38.504
he hated being tied down by any possessions...

00:09:40.914 --> 00:09:42.434
What's her problem!

00:09:43.014 --> 00:09:44.684
Hey, Miss Wakatake!

00:09:44.684 --> 00:09:47.014
Did you really live with your
grandmother all this time?

00:09:47.184 --> 00:09:48.354
What about your parents?

00:09:48.354 --> 00:09:50.154
You studied with private tutors?

00:09:50.154 --> 00:09:52.384
Where did you live before you came here?

00:09:52.624 --> 00:09:54.794
It's like the inquisition or something!

00:09:54.794 --> 00:09:55.824
Oh!

00:09:55.824 --> 00:09:57.384
We, uh...

00:09:57.794 --> 00:09:58.764
Um...

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:04.824
Excuse me, girls. Your physics reports
are due today. Don't forget!

00:10:05.134 --> 00:10:07.104
Oh, no!

00:10:07.104 --> 00:10:09.294
Physics is 6th period, right?

00:10:09.774 --> 00:10:12.304
We'll work on it during lunch, okay?

00:10:12.304 --> 00:10:14.104
Please, class president!

00:10:14.874 --> 00:10:16.244
I hope you make it!

00:10:16.244 --> 00:10:18.644
See you later, Mari!

00:10:18.914 --> 00:10:20.574
Sorry about that!

00:10:21.484 --> 00:10:24.074
Haven't they got anything better to do?

00:10:24.654 --> 00:10:29.214
Perhaps you should try to be a bit
more conscious of others.

00:10:29.554 --> 00:10:32.084
Everyone sure trusts you.

00:10:37.094 --> 00:10:39.264
But you can't fool me!

00:10:42.034 --> 00:10:44.634
W-What?

00:10:49.044 --> 00:10:50.604
What?!

00:10:51.744 --> 00:10:53.274
Nothing.

00:10:54.284 --> 00:10:56.214
What a weirdo!

00:11:05.324 --> 00:11:06.624
Yo.

00:11:07.024 --> 00:11:08.424
Move, will you?

00:11:11.034 --> 00:11:12.664
What's with her?

00:11:13.064 --> 00:11:16.064
Who knows what she's thinking!

00:11:22.444 --> 00:11:24.244
That's... Kozuki...

00:11:24.244 --> 00:11:25.444
Oops, sorry!

00:11:25.514 --> 00:11:28.104
Michiko Kozuki.

00:11:30.584 --> 00:11:32.074
Michiko!

00:11:32.384 --> 00:11:33.784
Michi!

00:11:38.394 --> 00:11:39.824
Michi!

00:11:42.394 --> 00:11:48.334
Mari? Are you talking to me?

00:11:48.974 --> 00:11:51.494
Let's have lunch together, Michi!

00:11:52.644 --> 00:11:54.804
"Michi," huh?

00:11:56.314 --> 00:12:00.004
Well, in any case, she's a lively one!

00:12:00.514 --> 00:12:03.504
Oh, yes. She's fun to watch.

00:12:08.224 --> 00:12:09.914
What is it?

00:12:10.794 --> 00:12:12.224
Oh, nothing.

00:12:22.574 --> 00:12:26.374
How was school, Miss Wakatake?

00:12:28.344 --> 00:12:29.514
Um...

00:12:29.514 --> 00:12:30.544
Hmm?

00:12:30.544 --> 00:12:35.104
Oh, sorry. Would you mind calling
me by my first name?

00:12:36.054 --> 00:12:39.284
You mean "Mari?"

00:12:39.624 --> 00:12:44.754
Yes. I'm just not used to being called Wakatake.

00:12:45.164 --> 00:12:47.954
It just doesn't seem like me.

00:12:48.664 --> 00:12:56.404
But I have a vague memory of being called
Mari before... At least I think so.

00:12:57.804 --> 00:12:59.244
Memory?

00:12:59.974 --> 00:13:06.504
Yes. I don't remember anything from before
I came to live with my grandmother.

00:13:07.144 --> 00:13:11.884
Remember that huge tsunami that
wiped out a whole island?

00:13:12.524 --> 00:13:15.354
I survived that disaster.

00:13:15.624 --> 00:13:18.454
But the shock made me lose my memory!

00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:30.724
I will continue to monitor the target subject,

00:13:39.744 --> 00:13:44.274
the sole survivor of the Kamioki Island disaster.

00:13:45.454 --> 00:13:47.474
Oh, no! Is it that really the time?

00:13:51.994 --> 00:13:53.794
Yes?

00:13:53.794 --> 00:13:56.334
There's a car waiting for you, Ma'am.

00:13:56.334 --> 00:13:59.364
Ah, yes! I'll be right there!

00:13:59.364 --> 00:14:01.534
Oh! Are you going on a trip?

00:14:01.534 --> 00:14:05.994
Er, just attending a workshop.
Excuse me, please.

00:14:12.344 --> 00:14:14.584
Mari! Stay with us, Mari!

00:14:14.584 --> 00:14:17.954
I woke up the face of a worried old woman.

00:14:17.954 --> 00:14:21.614
She's regaining consciousness.
Take her vitals and find me a vein.

00:14:21.854 --> 00:14:23.384
Yes, sir.

00:14:24.194 --> 00:14:33.154
I didn't even know she was my grandmother
until later. I forgot my name, even.

00:14:34.704 --> 00:14:35.634
Oh, Mari!

00:14:35.634 --> 00:14:37.234
Hmm?

00:14:38.004 --> 00:14:44.314
I hope get your memory back some day!

00:14:46.244 --> 00:14:49.014
Oh... thank you.

00:14:49.854 --> 00:14:54.944
But you know, I've never really minded.

00:14:55.994 --> 00:15:02.154
I just wanted to go on living a
quiet life with my grandmother.

00:15:05.834 --> 00:15:08.804
You hate this school, don't you?

00:15:10.734 --> 00:15:15.764
I don't hate it. You're pretty fun
to be around, Michi!

00:15:16.374 --> 00:15:20.514
Um, about calling me Michi...

00:15:20.514 --> 00:15:24.574
I wasn't sure what to do when they
started interrogating me, though!

00:15:25.154 --> 00:15:27.624
There sure are a lot of weirdos around here!

00:15:27.694 --> 00:15:31.024
Especially that girl I sit next to!

00:15:31.724 --> 00:15:34.494
Miss Senkoji?

00:15:34.494 --> 00:15:38.124
What's her deal! She'd better watch it!

00:15:39.064 --> 00:15:40.604
From Novaal?

00:15:40.604 --> 00:15:44.804
They've been calling for you quite
persistently. What shall I do?

00:15:45.474 --> 00:15:47.204
Ignore them.

00:15:47.404 --> 00:15:51.534
But, this is the first time since we left Arume...

00:15:51.684 --> 00:15:57.484
Mutual communication was supposed to be
forbidden. Pay them no mind.

00:15:59.284 --> 00:16:00.754
Very well.

00:16:04.964 --> 00:16:06.924
Maybe you're making too much of this...

00:16:06.924 --> 00:16:10.054
No way! That's not true!

00:16:11.464 --> 00:16:14.694
She's not the type to do that sort of thing.

00:16:15.174 --> 00:16:18.974
It must be a misunderstanding... Mari?

00:16:21.514 --> 00:16:23.344
If you don't believe me...

00:16:23.774 --> 00:16:25.114
See if I care!

00:16:25.114 --> 00:16:26.474
Mari!

00:16:28.384 --> 00:16:31.014
Please, wait! Mari!

00:16:31.584 --> 00:16:32.924
Mari!

00:16:32.924 --> 00:16:34.324
Forget it!

00:16:34.324 --> 00:16:36.454
But...

00:16:37.194 --> 00:16:40.524
Yes. It's her.

00:16:41.134 --> 00:16:42.824
She's the one...

00:16:46.664 --> 00:16:49.194
May I have a word, Dorm Chief?

00:16:49.874 --> 00:16:52.234
Oh, Hagino! What's up?

00:16:53.504 --> 00:16:56.104
It's about Ms. Wakatake.

00:16:59.684 --> 00:17:03.484
Sheesh, what a pain.
How come we always have to...

00:17:04.054 --> 00:17:05.414
Come in!

00:17:06.524 --> 00:17:08.044
Um, Mari?

00:17:08.424 --> 00:17:09.894
Er...

00:17:11.224 --> 00:17:13.324
This can't be! It can't!

00:17:13.324 --> 00:17:15.054
Lady Hagino!

00:17:15.564 --> 00:17:17.054
Shh! Here she comes!

00:17:20.434 --> 00:17:21.634
Huh?

00:17:21.634 --> 00:17:26.244
Hagino Senkoji of the 11th Grade
Cherry Blossoms Class

00:17:26.244 --> 00:17:35.314
is to transfer to the right side in Room 5, Floor 2,
sharing the room with its current resident.

00:17:35.314 --> 00:17:38.484
Blue Sea Dorm Chief Hiroko Funatsumaru.

00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:40.784
Well, so what?

00:17:40.884 --> 00:17:47.024
Room 5, Floor 2... that's your room, Mari!

00:17:47.664 --> 00:17:48.994
So that means...

00:17:49.764 --> 00:17:54.424
You and Miss Senkoji will be roommates.

00:17:55.504 --> 00:17:57.234
You've got to be kidding!

00:18:05.514 --> 00:18:08.814
That was a pretty drastic move.

00:18:10.954 --> 00:18:17.014
It was Senkoji's request.
She wants to help Mari get adjusted.

00:18:17.554 --> 00:18:19.024
Oh?

00:18:19.294 --> 00:18:24.894
You know, Hagino's a bit too perfect.
Nothing ever fazes her...

00:18:28.674 --> 00:18:33.534
This is the first time I've ever
seen something affect her.

00:18:37.574 --> 00:18:39.484
I don't know what you're playing at...

00:18:39.484 --> 00:18:41.854
But if you ever disrespect Lady Hagino...

00:18:41.854 --> 00:18:43.784
You'll have to answer to us!

00:18:46.824 --> 00:18:51.424
I can really handle these myself!
It's so kind of you to help!

00:18:51.424 --> 00:18:52.764
It's our pleasure!

00:18:52.764 --> 00:18:55.294
We're honored to help, Lady Hagino!

00:18:55.294 --> 00:18:58.324
Say the word, anytime!

00:18:59.234 --> 00:19:00.264
Thank you.

00:19:00.264 --> 00:19:01.664
Sure!

00:19:05.804 --> 00:19:08.404
Good night, Lady Hagino!

00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:10.974
Thank you very much.

00:19:11.184 --> 00:19:12.804
Good night, girls.

00:19:14.144 --> 00:19:17.114
Fine. I'll expose her lies!

00:19:26.764 --> 00:19:27.834
What is it?

00:19:27.834 --> 00:19:29.624
Novaal Ship One.

00:19:29.834 --> 00:19:32.994
Departing Trench One.

00:19:34.704 --> 00:19:36.174
What's happening?

00:19:49.854 --> 00:19:51.374
What do you want?

00:19:54.254 --> 00:19:57.284
Don't tell me you want to kill me!

00:20:03.364 --> 00:20:05.164
I...

00:20:05.164 --> 00:20:06.604
Never...

00:20:09.074 --> 00:20:10.624
Never again...

00:20:12.674 --> 00:20:19.274
Novaal is accelerating. Target destination
is our current location.

00:20:59.284 --> 00:21:02.384
Commander, Novaal is on the move!

00:21:10.764 --> 00:21:11.604
She...

00:21:11.604 --> 00:21:13.294
She can see me?!

00:21:15.404 --> 00:21:17.834
Who are you?

00:21:27.484 --> 00:21:29.314
What's going on?

00:21:29.914 --> 00:21:32.784
What on earth?!

00:21:33.284 --> 00:21:35.014
You saw, didn't you.

00:21:38.264 --> 00:21:39.724
You...

00:21:42.164 --> 00:21:43.594
No!

00:21:43.594 --> 00:21:45.464
No... Stay back!

00:21:45.964 --> 00:21:47.504
But why?

00:21:47.504 --> 00:21:49.904
Stay away! Stay away from me!

00:21:53.404 --> 00:21:54.104
No!

00:21:54.104 --> 00:21:56.204
Wait. Calm down.

00:22:14.794 --> 00:22:16.734
This is Kamioki Island.

00:22:18.464 --> 00:22:21.904
Supposedly it was wiped out by a tsunami.

00:22:22.134 --> 00:22:28.944
But in fact, even after a five-year investigation,
the true cause of the disaster remains unknown.

00:22:29.774 --> 00:22:31.434
Have a look at this.

00:22:36.514 --> 00:22:46.514
Of the 857 islanders, nearly all were killed. But
only 449... roughly half... drowned in the tsunami.

00:22:46.864 --> 00:22:50.954
The other 407 were already dead when it hit.

00:22:53.264 --> 00:22:57.064
They died in various ways, but put simply...

00:22:59.704 --> 00:23:00.974
It was murder.

00:23:03.474 --> 00:23:04.774
I...

00:23:05.944 --> 00:23:07.274
I...

00:23:10.314 --> 00:23:12.944
What on earth...

00:23:14.654 --> 00:23:17.214
What on earth are you?!

00:23:29.034 --> 00:23:36.504
Futari narande te o tsunaida sora ni

00:23:37.314 --> 00:23:47.354
Mirai kasane chikau ano chiheisen

00:23:47.354 --> 00:23:55.024
Kaze ga yasashiku fuki nuketeku youni

00:23:55.734 --> 00:24:03.604
Bokura asu e toketetta

00:24:04.204 --> 00:24:07.804
Nagarete ku toki wa tada

00:24:07.804 --> 00:24:13.144
Shizuka ni kimi wo mimamotte

00:24:13.344 --> 00:24:17.084
Kanashimi mo "Sayonara" mo

00:24:17.084 --> 00:24:22.584
Aoi namida mo tsuyosa ni naru

00:24:23.924 --> 00:24:28.234
Bokura yume kakeru tsubomi

00:24:28.234 --> 00:24:33.064
Kotae sagashi ikiteku

00:24:33.064 --> 00:24:37.374
Hokori takaku saku hana ni

00:24:37.374 --> 00:24:43.074
Itsuka wa nareru to shinjiteta

00:24:43.074 --> 00:24:47.034
In the blue dreams!

00:25:01.864 --> 00:25:05.664
Hagino is summoned back to her ship.

00:25:07.034 --> 00:25:15.964
The Blue returns to action, filled with painful
memories... Mari's, Hagino's, and Azanael's.

00:25:17.014 --> 00:25:21.244
Amid their conflicting emotions,
the Blue surfaces.

00:25:22.914 --> 00:25:27.114
Next time on Blue Drop: Datura.
